/F1 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 736 Tm (Understanding Diffusion Models: A Minimal Reading Guide) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 706 Tm (Abstract) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 686.5 Tm (Diffusion models learn to generate data by gradually reversing a fixed noising process.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 671 Tm (Starting from pure Gaussian noise, a neural network is trained to predict the noise) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 655.5 Tm (added at each step, so that sampling becomes an iterative denoising procedure. This note) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 640 Tm (summarizes the core ideas for a first reading.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 618.5 Tm (1. The Forward Process) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 599 Tm (The forward process is a Markov chain that corrupts an image x0 over T steps with a) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 583.5 Tm (variance schedule. At each step, Gaussian noise is added according to q\(xt | xt-1\) =) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 568 Tm (N\(xt; sqrt\(1 - beta_t\) * xt-1, beta_t I\). A key algebraic property is that any) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 552.5 Tm (intermediate step can be sampled in closed form using the cumulative products alpha_t,) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 537 Tm (which makes training efficient because the model never needs to simulate the full chain.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 515.5 Tm (The noise schedule beta_t is typically small early and larger later. Choosing this) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 500 Tm (schedule is a bias-variance trade-off: too aggressive a schedule destroys semantic) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 484.5 Tm (structure before the network can learn it, while too conservative a schedule wastes) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 469 Tm (computation.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 447.5 Tm (2. The Reverse Process and Training Objective) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 428 Tm (The reverse process is also modeled as Gaussian, but its mean is produced by a U-Net) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 412.5 Tm (epsilon_theta. Ho et al. \(2020\) showed that predicting the noise itself, rather than the) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 397 Tm (mean, yields a simplified loss: L_simple = E || epsilon - epsilon_theta\(xt, t\) ||^2.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 381.5 Tm (This reweighting behaves like a form of denoising score matching and is the de facto) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 366 Tm (standard objective.) Tj
